-- title:
--   Supersingular component chart at q=3, existence and uniqueness
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, with residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\kappa$-algebra `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ M') \in \mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \kappa$. Let `hle` be the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, into `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring of the source, a surjective residue map onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction of constants in $A$, together with a degree- and order-preserving map on places), and assume $R_0$ is pinned: every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $s \in W$. Then there exist a field $F_{SS}$ that is an algebra over $\kappa$ and a component chart $C$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with values in $F_{SS}$, such that: (i) some element of $F_{SS}$ is transcendental over $\kappa$; (ii) for every $f$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lying in the integers of $R_0$, if $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation ring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` is $C$-integral and its $C$-residue is the image in $F_{SS}$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\ f) \in \kappa$; (iii) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, the chart obtained from $C$ by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` has the same valuation ring as $C$; and (iv) $C$ is unique in the following sense: any field $F'$ over $\kappa$ and component chart $C'$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with values in $F'$ satisfying the analogues of (i), (ii) and (iii) has the same valuation ring as $C$.
--
--   This is the existence and uniqueness, at the prime $q = 3$, of the supersingular (Drinfeld) component chart of the full-level modular curve lying over a prescribed supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ modular curve in characteristic $q$, pinned intrinsically by its interaction with $R_0$-integral level-$M'$ functions regular away from the cusps and by invariance of its valuation ring under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; the divisibility of $M'$ by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ serves as a rigidity guard on automorphisms of supersingular points. It feeds the construction of the semistable covering and semistable model of the full-level modular curve at $q = 3$.
